WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:04.040
Art, as it has been said, is often subjective.

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:09.290
Whether it’s a sculpture, an oil painting
from the Renaissance, a renowned work of literature,

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:15.310
a digitally drawn webcomic or an insightful
animated YouTube video about SCP Foundation

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:20.519
lore, the deeper meaning behind a piece of
art can often change depending on the individual

00:00:20.519 --> 00:00:21.869
observing it.

00:00:21.869 --> 00:00:26.659
Sometimes, an artist intentionally makes the
message of their artwork clear, hoping to

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:31.189
have its meaning be unmistakable to any and
all that might see it.

00:00:31.189 --> 00:00:37.450
Other times, such a meaning can be more ambiguous,
harder to decipher without some serious thought.

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:42.420
But either way, art is an important way that
human beings interpret the world around us.

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:49.580
It can be a reflection of emotions, experiences,
history and every new creation is as legitimate

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:52.080
a piece of art as the last.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:56.450
But even with that being said, there may be
no piece of art that is a better reflection

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:59.320
of the world around us than SCP-804.

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:05.400
Or, to use its alternative title, the World
Without Man.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:10.590
As you might have already guessed, SCP-804
is an art installation.

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:14.300
Or at the very least, it is what’s left
of an art installation.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:18.609
The piece itself which was unveiled in Alaska,
was created by a group of artists known by

00:01:18.609 --> 00:01:25.119
the name ‘Unelmat Paremmasta Maailmasta’,
A Finnish phrase which translates to ‘Dreams

00:01:25.119 --> 00:01:27.020
of a Better World’ in English.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:33.119
A fitting, highly appropriate name for the
group that created SCP-804, given the subject

00:01:33.119 --> 00:01:34.479
of the piece.

00:01:34.479 --> 00:01:39.159
All that remains of the artwork itself is
a portion of a once larger statue, sculpted

00:01:39.159 --> 00:01:41.499
to resemble the shape of a globe.

00:01:41.499 --> 00:01:46.530
Following extensive examination by the SCP
Foundation’s researchers, this globe has

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:51.189
been determined to most likely be a re-creation
of our very own Planet Earth.

00:01:51.189 --> 00:01:55.289
Originally, this globe was a large, clear
model of Earth that also featured a number

00:01:55.289 --> 00:01:58.560
of smaller globes and video equipment inside
of it.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:03.590
It appears then that this art installation
may have been intended to function as a projector

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:08.750
of sorts, displaying varying images of scenes
from around the world.

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:14.010
These images would have primarily focused
on deserted and run down areas of human society,

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:17.709
such as abandoned buildings and decaying landmarks.

00:02:17.709 --> 00:02:22.390
The art piece seems to have depicted how even
when we reshape our world and build cities,

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:26.180
we can damage the planet’s fragile ecosystem.

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:31.060
This is especially prevalent when the things
we build are then later left empty, buildings

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:38.709
rotting away, structures neglected to waste;
This mass destruction of nature, all in vain.

00:02:38.709 --> 00:02:42.879
These images would then have been contrasted
with projections that show parts of the natural

00:02:42.879 --> 00:02:48.260
world that have yet to be touched by human
beings, serene, beautiful places like corners

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:52.600
of the Amazon rainforest or the deepest stretches
of our oceans.

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:53.920
The message of the piece?

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:58.430
Well, we can only speculate, but it seems
as if it played a role in highlighting the

00:02:58.430 --> 00:03:01.159
difference between the modern and natural
world.

00:03:01.159 --> 00:03:05.659
So, what could be so important about one leftover
piece of a statue?

00:03:05.659 --> 00:03:11.940
How about this: when it was first unveiled,
SCP-804 was able to produce a massive destructive

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:15.720
force, one in which plenty of people were
present to witness.

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:20.430
The Foundation has uncovered a number of documents
about ‘World Without Man’ from the artists’

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:26.610
website, when they stepped in to clear up
what happened after SCP-804 was revealed.

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:30.750
Among those present when the piece was displayed
were an audience of prominent environmental

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:34.939
activists who were well known throughout the
world for their efforts to alert people to

00:03:34.939 --> 00:03:39.441
the threats facing our environment, and would
likely be the ones that the message of World

00:03:39.441 --> 00:03:42.109
Without Man would resonate with the most.

00:03:42.109 --> 00:03:46.390
Of course, we doubt the SCP Foundation is
all that interested in the artistic value

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:52.050
of SCP-804, or its message of protecting the
environment for that matter.

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:56.250
What happened next was probably more likely
to be what caught their interest.

00:03:56.250 --> 00:04:01.750
From the moment it was activated, SCP-804’s
destructive properties were unleashed, and

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:05.170
it is still unclear if this was intentional
or not.

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:10.610
Had the members of Unelmat Paremmasta Maailmasta
planned to unfurl chaos at the revealing of

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:15.970
their masterpiece, or was World Without Man
sabotaged by someone who disagreed with its

00:04:15.970 --> 00:04:17.239
deeper meaning?

00:04:17.239 --> 00:04:24.480
It’s hard to say, the only thing the Foundation
knows for certain is that no one survived.

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:28.850
Anyone present during the incident was killed
where they stood, and those responsible for

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:34.430
creating SCP-804 either went into hiding or
perished themselves.

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:40.420
When activated, the smaller globes within
SCP-804’s larger one begin to rotate, causing

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:44.479
the display of its destructive and anomalous
properties.

00:04:44.479 --> 00:04:49.810
The sculpture itself causes any man-made devices
or artifacts within a one hundred meter radius

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:51.380
to stop working.

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:57.420
Everything from phones and tablets, to clothing,
plastic, buildings, and even synthetic chemical

00:04:57.420 --> 00:05:03.010
compounds will begin to deteriorate, decay
and even disintegrate.

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:09.389
If something is more advanced than a sharpened
stick of wood, SCP-804 can destroy it.

00:05:09.389 --> 00:05:15.080
The longer World Without Man remains active,
the wider its area of effect, and the stronger

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:17.060
its destructive power will be.

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:23.020
However, its ability to destroy any man-made
object is always strongest closer to the source,

00:05:23.020 --> 00:05:25.890
right next to the globe of the sculpture.

00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:30.419
Sounds pretty inconvenient to be subjected
to losing your clothes and personal belongings

00:05:30.419 --> 00:05:34.919
if you stand too close, but still harmless,
right?

00:05:34.919 --> 00:05:35.919
Wrong.

00:05:35.919 --> 00:05:40.990
SCP-804 also has an adverse, destructive effect
on human beings.

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:45.020
Tissue cells will also deteriorate in the
same way if they are within the radius of

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:46.430
World Without Man.

00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:51.690
However, this happens much slower than when
the sculpture disintegrates man-made matter.

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:57.990
People standing too close will be painfully
and excruciatingly broken down, cell by cell.

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:05.270
A victim of SCP-804 will gradually lose body
mass, bit by bit, until only their skeleton

00:06:05.270 --> 00:06:06.270
remains.

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:08.260
But it does not stop there.

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:13.729
The effects of the anomalous art piece will
continue even after death, dissolving bone,

00:06:13.729 --> 00:06:20.470
organs, muscle, and marrow into their most
basic atomic components, until truly nothing

00:06:20.470 --> 00:06:21.470
remains.

00:06:21.470 --> 00:06:27.919
Interestingly, there are ways to survive an
encounter with the anomalous effect of SCP-804.

00:06:27.919 --> 00:06:31.470
The first is to, well, not be a human being.

00:06:31.470 --> 00:06:36.620
Anything non-human, including all forms of
animal and plant life, will be left unharmed

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:37.620
by the sculpture.

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:43.139
So, if you can somehow think of a quick way
to transform yourself into a bird, or a hydrangea,

00:06:43.139 --> 00:06:47.800
you would manage to escape unscathed, in theory
at least.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:53.349
Speaking of escaping, though, even if you
were caught in SCP-804’s area of effect,

00:06:53.349 --> 00:06:57.590
there is a chance you could still survive
if you got far enough away before your entire

00:06:57.590 --> 00:06:59.629
body was turned to dust.

00:06:59.629 --> 00:07:05.009
Though drastic, it is possible to recover
from World Without Man’s human tissue damage

00:07:05.009 --> 00:07:09.580
given the proper circumstances and volume
of medical care.

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:14.199
During the SCP Foundation’s testing, those
who have survived, have suffered symptoms

00:07:14.199 --> 00:07:18.160
similar to those of extreme and prolonged
starvation.

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:23.010
Creating a sculpture that sends out a shockwave
capable of destroying all man-made materials

00:07:23.010 --> 00:07:28.720
and any human beings within one hundred meters
of it’s source, is certainly one hell of

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:32.379
a way to get the deeper message of your artwork
across.

00:07:32.379 --> 00:07:39.139
But that might have you thinking, if SCP-804
is a piece of art, and it was created by the

00:07:39.139 --> 00:07:44.740
members of an art collective, then isn’t
World Without Man also technically man-made?

00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:47.439
And you would be correct in thinking that.

00:07:47.439 --> 00:07:53.159
Through prolonged testing of the device, the
SCP Foundation has determined that SCP-804

00:07:53.159 --> 00:07:56.800
is not immune to its own destructive effects.

00:07:56.800 --> 00:08:01.510
Since its first activation, and over the course
of the Foundation’s rigorous examination

00:08:01.510 --> 00:08:05.560
of it, the sculpture’s capabilities have
become impaired.

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:08.949
However, this does not make it any less dangerous.

00:08:08.949 --> 00:08:15.470
If someone was somehow able to repair SCP-804,
perhaps reunite it with the statue it was

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:21.830
originally a part of, then the threat it would
pose to the modern world would be astronomical.

00:08:21.830 --> 00:08:23.530
How bad would the damage be?

00:08:23.530 --> 00:08:29.330
Well, let’s put it this way; if SCP-804
was able to remain fully active without suffering

00:08:29.330 --> 00:08:35.010
its own effects, then this anomalous artwork
could easily wipe any and all traces of humanity

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:39.599
from the face of Planet Earth… in a matter
of weeks.

00:08:39.599 --> 00:08:44.229
You could be forgiven for thinking that destroying
man-made artifacts and disintegrating human

00:08:44.229 --> 00:08:50.260
tissue was the worst that SCP-804 can do,
but you would be wrong yet again.

00:08:50.260 --> 00:08:55.100
The Foundation’s top researchers have theorized
that World Without Man also possessed some

00:08:55.100 --> 00:09:01.801
form of memetic effect, that SCP-804 is able
to mentally influence people, possibly creating

00:09:01.801 --> 00:09:04.390
a compulsion among those who view it.

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:08.970
However, they are still uncertain of this,
and testing is currently focused on if this

00:09:08.970 --> 00:09:13.870
effect has also been weakened by SCP-804’s
gradual decay.

00:09:13.870 --> 00:09:17.060
But back to when this destructive piece of
art was first discovered.

00:09:17.060 --> 00:09:23.470
Unelmat Paremmasta Maailmasta had unveiled
World Without Man at an art show in Alaska.

00:09:23.470 --> 00:09:29.140
Around five minutes after SCP-804 initially
activated, a nearby remote town in northern

00:09:29.140 --> 00:09:31.980
Alaska was the first to feel the effects.

00:09:31.980 --> 00:09:37.570
The residents were panicked, calling for emergency
services - After all, wouldn’t you be afraid

00:09:37.570 --> 00:09:43.680
if you realized that you were starting to
disintegrate, along with your home and all

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:44.680
your possessions?

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:48.450
Unfortunately, the town was too remote of
a location for anyone to properly respond.

00:09:48.450 --> 00:09:53.360
A single light aircraft was the first on the
scene, and the pilot witnessed firsthand as

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:56.300
the entire town was rapidly wiped out.

00:09:56.300 --> 00:10:00.820
By the time the Foundation heard about the
situation and dispatched its agents to the

00:10:00.820 --> 00:10:03.430
location, there was nothing left.

00:10:03.430 --> 00:10:07.330
Not one home, nor any living person.

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:13.410
SCP-804 had been active for almost eight straight
hours, and the nearby Alaskan town had been

00:10:13.410 --> 00:10:17.760
wiped clean of any and all traces of human
civilization.

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:22.910
The Foundation’s agents traced the epicenter
of SCP-804’s destructive effect back to

00:10:22.910 --> 00:10:28.100
where it had been unveiled, only to discover
that survivors from the nearby town had gathered

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:30.779
around what was left of the sculpture.

00:10:30.779 --> 00:10:35.410
Many of them were already suffering from hypothermia,
as well as being severely affected by the

00:10:35.410 --> 00:10:36.980
device in other ways.

00:10:36.980 --> 00:10:43.510
Somehow, these survivors were being compelled
to approach SCP-804 and push the globe within

00:10:43.510 --> 00:10:45.380
to reactivate its effect.

00:10:45.380 --> 00:10:49.990
If one died, another would step forward from
the group to take their place.

00:10:49.990 --> 00:10:54.990
Those around the sculpture would cheer and
encourage them to maintain the anomalous artwork,

00:10:54.990 --> 00:11:00.570
praising them for keeping it running despite
what SCP-804 was doing to them.

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:05.160
Under the orders of an O5 council member,
the Foundation agents on site opened fire

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:10.089
on the crowd, their bullets disintegrating
from the statue’s effect but still managing

00:11:10.089 --> 00:11:12.220
to cause lethal wounds.

00:11:12.220 --> 00:11:17.630
As the globe stopped spinning, the effects
of SCP-804 ended and the agents were able

00:11:17.630 --> 00:11:20.300
to move in and secure the sculpture.

00:11:20.300 --> 00:11:25.180
Many of the survivors then opted to lie down
in the snow, letting their injuries and the

00:11:25.180 --> 00:11:26.889
cold kill them.

00:11:26.889 --> 00:11:31.139
Any that were arrested by the Foundation refused
to respond to questioning.

00:11:31.139 --> 00:11:37.350
Given that any Foundation facility would be
man-made in nature, it was decided that SCP-804

00:11:37.350 --> 00:11:42.760
would be best left where it was, allowing
the Alaskan cold to freeze its machinery.

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:47.839
A handful of Foundation guards were left on
site as well, just in case anyone decided

00:11:47.839 --> 00:11:53.339
to come looking for World Without Man and
try to reactivate the anomalous piece of art.

00:11:53.339 --> 00:11:57.880
Additionally, the Foundation wanted the remains
of the device kept away from their facilities

00:11:57.880 --> 00:12:02.709
until they could figure out if or how it had
compelled people to keep it active.

00:12:02.709 --> 00:12:09.410
Doctor Johannes Sorts of the SCP Foundation
investigated the memetic properties of SCP-804,

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:14.149
and according to his findings “There is
nothing especially virulent or dangerous about

00:12:14.149 --> 00:12:16.410
SCP-804's memetic properties.

00:12:16.410 --> 00:12:22.130
Only a few select personality types have any
desire to re-activate the device…

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:27.160
We've been looking at this all wrong, there
is no magical compulsion that could drive

00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:29.440
so many people to destroy themselves.

00:12:29.440 --> 00:12:31.649
There does not need to be.”

00:12:31.649 --> 00:12:36.889
The artist and activist group Unelmat Paremmasta
Maailmasta had created a device capable of

00:12:36.889 --> 00:12:40.540
wiping out all traces of human life on Earth.

00:12:40.540 --> 00:12:45.990
It could turn buildings and people to dust,
making any that were left keep it spinning

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:47.880
no matter if it killed them.

00:12:47.880 --> 00:12:54.089
It was made to represent an ideal, the cure
for the planet from the disease of humanity.

00:12:54.089 --> 00:12:59.080
But why would these activists unleash it on
a town full of innocent people?

00:12:59.080 --> 00:13:04.269
If they knew this machine had the potential
to wipe out all human life on Earth, why activate

00:13:04.269 --> 00:13:06.610
it, killing themselves too?

00:13:06.610 --> 00:13:11.450
The answer is simple: because they wanted
to.

00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:14.100
They intended to send a message.

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:18.940
But the real question is, are we smart enough
to listen to it?

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:24.970
Now go check out “SCP-2317 - The Devourer
of Worlds / A Door to Another World” and

00:13:24.970 --> 00:13:30.010
“SCP XK Class End of the World Scenarios
Explained” for more anomalies that could

00:13:30.010 --> 00:13:31.779
bring humanity to its knees!

